@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/sequence-diagram
title Branching model: trunk-based with promotion

participant "feat/95-...\n(worktree A)" as A
participant "fix/113-...\n(worktree B)" as B
participant "trunk" as T
participant "TEST" as TEST
participant "PROD" as PROD

T -> A : git worktree add
T -> B : git worktree add
A -> A : commits + changelog.d/feat-95-....md
B -> B : commits + changelog.d/fix-113-....md

A -> T : PR (CI only), squash merge
T -> TEST : build sha-a, deploy, release v1.3.0
B -> T : PR (CI only), squash merge
T -> TEST : build sha-b, deploy, release v1.3.1

note over T, PROD
  Approving the run of sha-a does nothing,
  because sha-b is already the newest build.
end note
TEST -> PROD : approve run of sha-b\n(retag sha-b as latest)

== Fix forward ==
T -> T : fix/... PR, squash merge
T -> TEST : build sha-c, deploy, release v1.3.2
TEST -> PROD : approve run of sha-c

== Rollback ==
PROD -> PROD : rollback.yml, version=1.3.1\n(retag 1.3.1 as latest)
@enduml
